# Pages this archive draws by hand on purpose. checkpages prints every line of
# this file on every run, so an exemption nobody can justify is an exemption
# somebody will notice.

namesakes: notable people who merely share the surname, each with a plate or a painting and a lightbox over the set. Booyzen's page of the same name is about repeated FORENAMES and Falco's argues for not having one. Three different pages wearing one name.
research-log: a QUESTION TRACKER — open, blocked and closed — not a log of work done. The page says so itself: the same questions are set out one at a time on /open-questions/, and this one is the summary view. Booyzen's and Luwinski's research logs are chronological narratives; Falco's is an index of working files.
dna: three tested people with admixture bars, a Y-DNA line, the «Notable Individuals» list and a MyHeritage AutoCluster table with its own five columns. The bars are a single distribution per person; Falco's are a side-by-side COMPARISON of two people across shared groups, which is a different chart answering a different question.
places/[slug]: an ENCYCLOPAEDIA ENTRY per place, not an index of what the atlas holds there. It carries the place's name in Croatian, Italian, German and Friulian, its parish and diocese, its population by year, its register holdings, a slice of the 1945 census and the photographic plates taken there. The kit's PlacePage answers a different question — who this archive can put in a place, and which registers and records cover it — which this archive answers on /atlas/.
